# firebase-config.js is NOT committed here. In the daringcomics app it was, and
# that was correct for a single deployed app. The shell is a starting point for
# many games: a pack copied from here must reach its OWN Firebase project, never
# inherit another one. Copy firebase-config.example.js and fill in your own.
# (The config still ships to every visitor of a built app — the controls are the
# API-key restrictions and the Realtime Database rules. See MULTIPLAYER.md §1.)
firebase-config.js

node_modules/

# Extraction intermediates. These hold raw text pulled straight out of the
# rulebook PDF on the way to building a pack's data files, which is prose that
# does not belong in the repo — the packs ship mechanics, not the book.
.*.json
.*.txt
.skills*
.creation*
.rc*
.spells*
.vocab*
